3800:
** ὀψώνιον**, τό,
(ὄψον, ὠνέομαι) **salary**, reckoned in money, τό τε ὀ. καὶ σιτομετρίαν καὶ τὸ ἔλαιον {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PCair.Zen.” 507.5, compare 421.6, 483.14, 498.5 (all 3rd c.BC); ἵνα ἡμῖν ὀ. προστεθῇ καὶ σιτάριον [prev. work] 49.4 (3rd c.BC)}}; μετρήματα καὶ ὀ. corn- and **money**-payments, {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|“UPZ” 14.26 (2nd c.BC)}}; φυλακιτῶν {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PPetr.” 3p.230 (3rd c.BC)}}; of a bank clerk, {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PCair.Zen.” 342.6 (3rd c.BC): distinguished from γραμματικόν (bonus on turnover), “PStrassb.” 105.4 (3rd c.BC)}}; χωρὶς ὀψωνίων, of un**salaried** services, {{Refs 1st c.BC+|“Inscription Prien.” 121.34 (1st c.BC).}}
**2** a policeman's **pay,** {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|PLille 25.55 (3rd c.BC), “PFay.” 302 (2nd c.BC), “IG” 9(2).1109.27 (Thess., 2nd-1st c.BC)}}; frequently a soldier's **pay,** {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|PStrassb. 103.16 (3rd c.BC), “PTheb.Bank” 6.7 (2nd c.BC), 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 6.39.12}}: so in _plural_, **pay** of an army, {{LXX+4th c.BC+|“Rev.Ét.Anc.” 33.8 (Theangela, 4th-3rd c.BC), “OGI” 229.106 (3rd c.BC), “SIG” 410.19 (3rd c.BC), 581.34 (2nd-1st c.BC), 2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 1.67.1, 3.25.4, LXX.1Mac.3.28, Aristeas 22.}}
**3** **allowance** paid to a victorious athlete, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|“PRyl.” 153.25 (2nd c.AD), “CPHerm.” 54.7, +others (3rd c.AD)}}; **allowance** or **scholarship** paid to a music-student, προδοῦναί μοι τὸ ὀ. καὶ τὸ κατὰ μῆνα ἀνάλωμα {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PCair.Zen.” 440.6 (3rd c.BC)}}; **allowance** to a son or daughter, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|“BGU” 665 ii 15 (1st c.AD), “POxy.” 898.31 (2nd c.AD)}}; to a slave, distinguished from ἱματις μός, {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|“PCair.Zen.” 28.6, 100.14 (3rd c.BC).}}
**4** **wages** of labour, τὰ σώματα ἐνοχλεῖ ἡμᾶς τὰ ὀ. ἀπαιτοῦντα {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|[prev. work] 43.2, compare 27.2, +others, “PPetr.” 2p.113 (all 3rd c.BC), “POxy.” 974 (3rd c.AD)}}; ἀρτάβην κριθῆς εἰς λόγον ὀψωνίων {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|“PTeb.” 420.24 (3rd c.AD): _metaphorically_, ὀψώνια ἁμαρτίας}} the **wages** of sin, {{NT|NT.Rom.6.23.}}
**5** a magician's **fee,** {{Refs|PMag.Par. 1.2454.}}
**6** **gratuity** to tax-farmers, {{Refs|“UPZ” 112v3 (_plural_).}}
**7** ={ὄψον} {{Refs|I.1 (cf. Latin}}**obsonium**), τῶν ἀνηλωμάτων πάντων σίτου καὶ ὀψωνίων {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|[prev. work] 91.13 (2nd c.BC).}}—The word is rejected by {{Refs 4th c.BC+|2nd c.AD: Phrynichus Atticista 393. First used by 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 1051 (no context); ᾔτησεν εἰς ὀ. τριώβολον Thugenides Comicus 2. Glossed ὀψωνία, also (in _plural_) κέρδη, χαρίσματα, by 9th c.AD: Photius Legal icographus, etc.}}

